d-precision `created_at` after the captured `now`. Any second-boundary crossing trips it. Worth its own item against `internal/registry`.\n2. The conformance vectors that would cross-check the identity change skip as `root-unset` on **every** lane including ubuntu — pre-existing gate gap.\n3. **`BUG-260731-33v6zz`'s description is wrong:** it claims none of its 14 cases appear in `platform-cases.tsv`, but `main` carries 7 `cmd/curator` rows (lines 149–155) and the gate reports all 7 as required-case failures. Fix that scope before it starts.\n4. No CHANGELOG entry for a user-facing fix — though PRs 9/10/11 also skipped it and nothing enforces it.\n\n`Test (windows-latest)` remains red only on those 7 `cmd/curator` rows, exactly as the ownership map predicted. Logbook entry appended (`LOGBOOK.md` is modified but uncommitted).","ttft_ms":3096,"ttft_stream_ms":2758,"time_to_request_ms":25,"type":"result","duration_ms":1577741,"uuid":"a05bbf45-22e2-4eb0-8f99-6f83e9515737"}
